WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.230
In 1785, two books on morality appeared.

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.170
In one, Immanuel Kant
built ethics on duty.

3
00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:12.970
In the other, William Paley argued
that God wills human happiness.

4
00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:16.340
So we find God's will by weighing results.

5
00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:20.380
Kant even puzzled over Jesus'
command to love your enemy.

6
00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.490
Can a feeling be ordered?

7
00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.960
So does Christian ethics
follow rules, weigh results,

8
00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.470
or build character?

9
00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.350
And who gets to say?

10
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.840
In this mission, you'll test
Christian ideas against Kant,

11
00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:36.240
Bentham and virtue ethics, card by card.

12
00:00:36.290 --> 00:00:39.200
Then you'll meet thinkers
from Aquinas to Fletcher,

13
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:42.730
and see how secular ideas
have shaped Christian thought.

14
00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:46.410
Your mission: work out whether
Christian ethics follows rules,

15
00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:50.290
weighs results or builds
character, and who decides.
